~ intro
Narrator: The Hollowmarch. Three nights since the last star went dark above the old road.
Narrator: Four strangers share a dying fire at the forest's edge.
Brokk: Right. Ground rules. Nobody touches my arrows. Nobody touches my book.
Average: What about your beard?
Brokk: ESPECIALLY not the beard.
Puck: Guys. Look up. There's, like... a hole where the moon goes.
Eowilas: The cult of the Hollow Moth. They're snuffing out the stars, one shrine at a time.
Nana: And you four are going to stop them. I've decided.
Puck: Nana's decided. That's binding, legally.
- Then we go together.
	Average: Together! Behind me. Mostly behind me.
- Who leads?
	Eowilas: Whoever walks first. The rest of us follow, and keep them alive.
	Brokk: Mostly alive.
Narrator: Somewhere past the gallows, a bell tolls with no one to ring it.
=> END

~ boss_intro
Narrator: The pit stinks of rust and old fire. Something huge unfolds from the ash.
Brokk: That's a lot of armour for one skeleton.
Average: Finally. Someone my size.
Eowilas: Careful. There's a soul burning inside him, chained to the iron.
Nana: Puck, sweetheart, stay behind the big one.
Puck: Always do, Nana.
=> END

~ boss_dead
Narrator: The Iron Brother sinks to his knees. The fire in his joints gutters out.
Eowilas: Whoever you were... you're free now.
Average: I WON! ...We won. Mostly me.
Brokk: Iron Brother. Page one. Crossed out.
Puck: Hey. Hey, look up. A star just came back.
=> END

~ shrine_first
Nana: Oh, a Moth Shrine. Come here, all of you. Let me look at you.
Nana: You're tired, you're filthy and someone is bleeding on my good ghost-shawl.
- Rest here, Nana. We need it.
	Nana: Good. Sit. The moths will keep watch.
- We can't stop. The stars are going out.
	Nana: And they'll still be going out after you've had a sit-down.
Eowilas: She's right. The shrine will remember us if we fall.
Puck: Wait, so if we die we come back here?
Brokk: Hope you like this view. You'll see it a lot.
=> END

~ rift_enter
Narrator: The rift hums. Beyond it, ash falls upward into a red sky.
Eowilas: That's where the stars went. I can feel them, behind the smoke.
Brokk: Of course it's on fire. It's always on fire.
Puck: Nana, are you coming?
Nana: Sweetheart, I'm dead. I go where I please.
- Step through.
	Average: ME FIRST.
- One last look back.
	Puck: Bye, nice gloomy forest. You were the good kind of gloomy.
	Average: ME FIRST.
=> END

~ act2_intro
Narrator: The Cinderveil. A land where the sky burned down and nobody swept up.
Brokk: Smells like my uncle's forge. Before the fire. And after the fire.
Eowilas: The Iron Brother wasn't the master here. He was the jailer.
Average: Then who's the prisoner?
Narrator: Far to the north, something enormous rattles its chains.
Puck: ...Was that thunder?
Nana: That, my darling, was breathing.
- Then we find it.
	Eowilas: Carefully. Three wardens hold this place. Two of them still guard the way.
- Maybe we go back?
	Brokk: The rift closed behind us. I checked. Twice.
Puck: Okay. Shrine first. Shrine is always first.
=> END

~ wraith_intro
Narrator: Broken mirrors line the hall. Every shard shows a face that isn't yours.
Puck: Uh. Why am I old in that one?
Narrator: A pale woman steps out of the glass. She is weeping.
Eowilas: A mourner. She lost her own face and keeps stealing others.
Average: She can have mine. It's the best one.
Brokk: Mirrors lie. Hit the one that bleeds.
=> END

~ wraith_dead
Narrator: The Glass Mourner shatters. For a moment every mirror shows her as she was: smiling.
Eowilas: Rest now. Your face is your own again.
Puck: That was the saddest fight I've ever won.
Brokk: Glass Mourner. Crossed out. ...Gently.
=> END

~ moth_intro
Narrator: The grove is silent. Then every dead branch takes flight.
Eowilas: No. Oh, no. That's her shadow. The Black Butterfly's own shadow.
Puck: Your goddess has a shadow? Does she know?
Eowilas: She let it go so she could be free. Someone caught it and made it hungry.
Nana: Breathe through your sleeves, children. That dust is nasty.
Average: I will punch the dust.
=> END

~ moth_dead
Narrator: The great dark wings come apart into a thousand small moths. They are only moths now.
Eowilas: Go on. You're free. Find her again.
Puck: One of them landed on me. I'm keeping him. His name is Gary.
Brokk: You are not keeping a moth.
Puck: Gary stays.
=> END

~ dragon_intro
Narrator: The throne is a mountain of bones. Chains as thick as trees run up into the smoke.
Narrator: At the top, a dragon lifts its head. Its ribs glow like a furnace.
Brokk: That. That is page one. That has always been page one.
Average: My father told stories about a dragon on a chain. I thought he made it up.
Eowilas: Ashmaw. It's been eating the stars to stay warm.
Nana: Well. Somebody tell it dinner's over.
Puck: Not it.
=> END

~ dragon_dead
Narrator: Ashmaw falls. The chains go slack and ring like bells, one last time.
Narrator: Out of its burning chest, the lost stars rise. One. Then hundreds.
Puck: Guys. Guys, look up.
Average: I killed a DRAGON. Dad. DAD. Did you see that?
Brokk: Ashmaw. Crossed out. ...I need a new book.
Eowilas: The night is whole again. She would be proud of you. All of you.
=> END

~ rift_enter_2
Narrator: The second rift is cold. Frost creeps out of it and over the ash.
Eowilas: The stars Ashmaw freed... they didn't go home. Something called them down.
Brokk: Something worse than a dragon. Wonderful. I'll need a bigger book.
Nana: I know that cold. I felt it once. Right at the very end.
Puck: Nana? What do you mean, the end?
Nana: Walk, sweetheart. I'll tell you on the other side.
- Step through.
	Average: ME FIRST. Again.
- Hold Nana's hand.
	Puck: You're freezing.
	Nana: I'm dead, darling. But thank you.
=> END

~ act3_intro
Narrator: The Starfall Mere. A frozen lake under a black sky, and in the ice, every fallen star.
Puck: They're trapped. All of them. Like flies in honey.
Eowilas: Not trapped. Stored. Something is keeping them for later.
Nana: The Hollowmoth. It eats light. It ate the lamps of our village, then the moon over it.
Nana: Then it ate me. I went out like a candle, and woke up beside a little elf who wouldn't stop crying.
Puck: ...You never told me that.
Nana: You never needed to know. Now you do.
Average: Then I will punch it TWICE. Once for the stars. Once for Nana.
Brokk: Pages one, two and three. Page four is blank. I've been saving it.
- Then we end it.
	Eowilas: The Lantern Warden guards the shore. The Pale Choir sings it to sleep. Then the Hollowmoth.
- Is everyone ready?
	Puck: No. Let's go anyway.
=> END

