~ banter3_2
Puck: There's a star under my feet. It's blinking at me.
Eowilas: It knows you. Every star knows a little of everyone.
Puck: Hi, star. I'll get you out. Promise.
=> END

~ banter3_3
Brokk: My beard has frozen solid. I could chop wood with it.
Average: Can I try?
Brokk: No.
=> END

~ banter3_4
Nana: When I was alive, I used to skate on a lake like this.
Puck: Were you good at it?
Nana: Terrible. Your grandfather married me anyway.
=> END

~ banter3_5
Eowilas: Black Butterfly, if you're listening, we could use a little light.
Narrator: A single moth lands on her shoulder. It glows, faintly.
Puck: ...Is that Gary?
=> END

~ banter3_6
Average: After this, I want soup. Hot soup. A whole bucket.
Brokk: For once, lad, I agree with every word.
=> END

~ warden_intro
Narrator: A giant in rusted armour stands on the shore, holding a lantern full of stolen starlight.
Average: He looks like... no. It can't be.
Brokk: The Iron Brother had a brother. Of course he did. Families are always the worst.
Eowilas: The Lantern Warden. He feeds the Hollowmoth one star at a time.
Average: Then let's put out his lantern.
=> END

~ warden_dead
Narrator: The lantern cracks. A single star floats free and hangs over the lake like a little moon.
Puck: One down. About a million to go.
Brokk: Lantern Warden. Crossed out. In ink, this time.
=> END

~ choir_intro
Narrator: Pale figures stand in a ring on the ice. They are singing, and the song is a lullaby.
Puck: I'm... so... sleepy...
Nana: PUCK. Bite your tongue. Not literally. Well, a little bit literally.
Eowilas: The Pale Choir. They sing the stars to sleep so they don't fight back.
Average: I can't sing. But I can shout. AAAAAAH!
=> END

~ choir_dead
Narrator: The song breaks off mid-note. Under the ice, the stars begin to stir.
Eowilas: They're waking up. They can hear us now.
Puck: I'm awake too. Mostly.
Brokk: Choir. Crossed out. Worst concert of my life.
=> END

~ hollow_intro
Narrator: At the centre of the Mere the ice is gone. Something rises out of the black water.
Narrator: Wings as wide as a church. Where its face should be, there is only a hole full of night.
Nana: There you are. You took my lamp. You took my moon. You took me.
Puck: You don't get to take anything else.
Eowilas: Black Butterfly, this is the shadow you lost. Let us bring it home.
Brokk: Page four.
Average: FOR NANA!
=> END

~ hollow_dead
Narrator: The Hollowmoth tears open. Every star it swallowed pours out at once.
Narrator: The ice shatters. The Mere fills with light, and the light rises.
Puck: Nana... Nana, you're glowing.
Nana: I know, sweetheart. It gave back everything it took. Even me. A little.
Brokk: The Hollowmoth. Crossed out. ...Book's full. Good.
Average: Did we win? We won. I'm going to cry. Heroically.
=> END

~ ending
Nana: Look at my four. Frozen. Singed. Still standing.
Nana: The stars are back where they belong, and so is my light. I can go now, if you'll let me.
Puck: ...Will you come back?
Nana: Look up on a clear night. Find the one that's blinking at you. That's me, telling you to eat properly.
Eowilas: Go in peace, Nana. The Black Butterfly will carry you.
Average: Bye, Nana. Thank you for the shouting.
Brokk: There's a page for you, you know. In the other book. It just says "Nana. Kept us alive."
Narrator: And beneath a sky full of stars, one brighter than the rest, the party walked home.
Narrator: THE END.
Narrator: A game by DorkTeach.
=> END
